# L §5.10 (round 7c) `unit(x) == PLN` compares two keys: konto (PLN), k_eur (EUR) and h (etf, a key of the unit kind
# funds) are not outside; q1 counts the places whose unit is the key PLN: konto, 1; q2 the key EUR: k_eur, 1. q3 reads
# unit(world), a place of unit any: "a place of unit any has no one unit, and unit(x) of it is refused (§8.4)".
=== uk.tally
model uk
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
kind funds: unit

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place k_eur: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..
place h: holdings etf lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

ask q1: count(x in places over .. where not x in outside and unit(x) == PLN)
ask q2: count(x in places over .. where not x in outside and unit(x) == EUR)
ask q3: count(x in places over .. where unit(x) == PLN)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  funds + [etf] lives 2026-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k_eur] = 0 EUR at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q1: 1
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 1
  cut 2026-12-31
q3: refused: RUN-DOMAIN unit(world) of a place of unit any: it has no one unit
  cut 2026-12-31
